We consider 2D arrays $A$, (0,0)-indexed, shape $N \times M$. With $ 0 \le i < N $ and $ 0 \le j < M $, we have $ 0< A_{i,j} \le N \times M $. Our interest will be to count those arrays that have the two properties :
Arrays $A$ are composed with all numbers from $1$ to $N \times M$. i.e. we have $ (i,j) \neq (k,l) \implies A_{i,j} \neq A_{k,l} $ $(i\oplus j) > (k\oplus l) \implies A_{i,j} > A_{k,l} $, where $ \oplus $ denotes bitwise XOR.

